>> MADAM Clerk, can you please

00:11:03.108 --> 00:11:03.909
call item 18 item 18.

00:11:03.909 --> 00:11:04.543
This is a resolution to urge

00:11:04.543 --> 00:11:06.943
the implementation of a

00:11:07.446 --> 00:11:08.213
comprehensive and severe drug

00:11:08.213 --> 00:11:10.613
market intervention strategy to

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.550
address san francisco fentanyl

00:11:15.621 --> 00:11:16.456
crisis supervisor mahmud.

00:11:16.456 --> 00:11:18.456
>> thank you PRESIDENT

00:11:19.392 --> 00:11:20.920
Randleman and thank you

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:20.726
colleagues for the opportunity

00:11:20.726 --> 00:11:23.126
to have this resolution

00:11:23.328 --> 00:11:23.996
introduced.

00:11:23.996 --> 00:11:26.996
First I wanted to thank

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:27.766
PRESIDENT Milliman supervisors

00:11:27.766 --> 00:11:30.166
dorsey, cheryl and guardian

00:11:30.436 --> 00:11:30.969
sadr for their co-sponsorship

00:11:30.969 --> 00:11:32.969
on this resolution.

00:11:34.441 --> 00:11:35.174
>> this resolution was created

00:11:35.174 --> 00:11:38.174
because the tenderloin where I

00:11:38.945 --> 00:11:39.312
represent is home to over 3500

00:11:39.312 --> 00:11:41.312
children.

00:11:42.415 --> 00:11:43.149
>> yet these youth face

00:11:43.149 --> 00:11:45.149
unmanageable circumstances from

00:11:46.819 --> 00:11:47.553
witnessing overdoses to as

00:11:47.553 --> 00:11:50.223
we've seen in recent reports

00:11:50.223 --> 00:11:50.690
being coerced into the drug

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:51.391
trade as well.

00:11:51.391 --> 00:11:53.791
>> the fentanyl crisis has

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:55.695
created an unsafe environment

00:11:55.695 --> 00:11:58.950
for families and children

00:11:59.320 --> 00:11:59.799
and shifted our perception on a

00:11:59.799 --> 00:12:03.399
national scale to one that does

00:12:03.503 --> 00:12:03.903
not capture the heart and soul

00:12:03.903 --> 00:12:04.670
of the city.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.806
>> so many of us in this board

00:12:06.806 --> 00:12:07.574
are working to uplift what's

00:12:07.574 --> 00:12:10.574
happening on our streets cannot

00:12:10.711 --> 00:12:11.311
become the status quo.

00:12:11.311 --> 00:12:11.978
And every child in san

00:12:11.978 --> 00:12:14.378
francisco deserves a safe

00:12:15.248 --> 00:12:15.949
and healthy childhood and every

00:12:15.949 --> 00:12:18.349
resident and visitor deserves

00:12:19.219 --> 00:12:19.519
to feel safe and welcome in our

00:12:19.519 --> 00:12:20.119
city.

00:12:20.119 --> 00:12:22.119
>> we've tried different

00:12:22.455 --> 00:12:23.189
approaches in this city to

00:12:23.189 --> 00:12:24.230
address this crisis and it's

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.940
not for a lack of will or

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:27.728
resources but we have to be

00:12:27.728 --> 00:12:30.128
honest that there's more

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.167
progress that we have to take

00:12:34.167 --> 00:12:34.901
and we need new approaches.

00:12:34.901 --> 00:12:35.435
The drug market intervention

00:12:35.435 --> 00:12:37.435
resolution offers a

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:39.772
comprehensive and community

00:12:39.772 --> 00:12:42.509
driven approach from the supply

00:12:42.509 --> 00:12:43.177
side of this problem to

00:12:43.177 --> 00:12:45.577
dismantling open air drug

00:12:45.879 --> 00:12:46.347
markets while creating pathways

00:12:46.347 --> 00:12:46.847
for prevention

00:12:46.847 --> 00:12:48.847
and intervention.

00:12:50.517 --> 00:12:53.687
>> and this was born out of

00:12:53.687 --> 00:12:54.521
advocacy from the community

00:12:54.521 --> 00:12:57.390
from families at two one turn

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.258
to nonprofits two academics who

00:12:58.258 --> 00:13:01.295
came to us and said we have to

00:13:01.295 --> 00:13:02.196
focus on evidence.

00:13:02.196 --> 00:13:02.830
We have to focus on the data

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:05.230
that has been successful

00:13:05.366 --> 00:13:06.660
in tackling open air drug

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:06.733
markets across the country.

00:13:06.733 --> 00:13:08.733
Organizations like united

00:13:09.603 --> 00:13:12.572
players or the families at 2a1

00:13:12.572 --> 00:13:13.340
term nonprofits like mission

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:16.576
hiring hall have all said that

00:13:16.576 --> 00:13:17.278
they endorse this framework of

00:13:17.278 --> 00:13:17.979
a drug market intervention.

00:13:17.979 --> 00:13:20.979
And what this resolution is

00:13:21.449 --> 00:13:22.149
asking for is that we need

00:13:22.149 --> 00:13:22.783
specialists to come in and

00:13:22.783 --> 00:13:24.783
guide city departments,

00:13:25.319 --> 00:13:25.986
diagnose the situation

00:13:25.986 --> 00:13:28.956
and prescribe a roadmap for

00:13:28.956 --> 00:13:29.723
implementing a uniquely

00:13:29.723 --> 00:13:32.426
tailored solution for our city.

00:13:32.426 --> 00:13:34.826
There's three main components

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:36.130
here which is one collaboration

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:38.700
to it across different city

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:39.500
departments because it's not

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.168
just sfpd that is involved with

00:13:40.168 --> 00:13:43.370
the open air drug market.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:43.771
It's also department of public

00:13:43.771 --> 00:13:44.171
works, department of emergency

00:13:44.171 --> 00:13:46.171
management.

00:13:46.807 --> 00:13:47.408
So many organizations that have

00:13:47.408 --> 00:13:49.808
to be working together

00:13:50.177 --> 00:13:50.511
in concert to solve this

00:13:50.511 --> 00:13:51.178
problem.

00:13:51.178 --> 00:13:53.178
>> it involves deterrence

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:54.849
because as the drug markets are

00:13:54.849 --> 00:13:57.786
dismantled, we have to prevent

00:13:57.786 --> 00:13:58.386
new ones from emerging.

00:13:58.386 --> 00:13:58.987
And so this resolution

00:13:58.987 --> 00:14:00.987
prioritizes funding for

00:14:01.956 --> 00:14:03.956
community ambassador programs

00:14:04.559 --> 00:14:05.228
that provide alternative paths

00:14:05.228 --> 00:14:07.628
for first time nonviolent

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:09.765
offenders reducing recidivism

00:14:09.765 --> 00:14:12.165
and improving public safety.

00:14:12.434 --> 00:14:13.168
Prevention through community

00:14:13.168 --> 00:14:15.568
engagement is critical because

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:17.772
we need stronger workforce

00:14:17.772 --> 00:14:18.506
and youth development programs

00:14:18.506 --> 00:14:21.420
to provide alternatives to the

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:21.709
drug trade that we're seeing

00:14:21.709 --> 00:14:22.410
being exposed to our kids.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.810
This could involve investments

00:14:25.113 --> 00:14:25.880
in safe passage mentorship

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.817
programs, job training to break

00:14:28.817 --> 00:14:29.251
the cycle of crime

00:14:29.251 --> 00:14:31.251
and addiction.

00:14:32.487 --> 00:14:33.355
The impact of the fentanyl

00:14:33.355 --> 00:14:34.122
crisis it's not just on the

00:14:34.122 --> 00:14:34.623
individuals as we've indicated,

00:14:34.623 --> 00:14:36.623
it's on families

00:14:36.858 --> 00:14:37.626
and communities and we cannot

00:14:37.626 --> 00:14:40.562
allow another generation of san

00:14:40.562 --> 00:14:41.396
franciscans to grow up thinking

00:14:41.396 --> 00:14:44.500
that the drug trade is their

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.100
only option during our public

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:45.768
safety and neighborhood

00:14:45.768 --> 00:14:47.768
services committee meeting.

00:14:48.404 --> 00:14:49.104
>> I introduced an amendment on

00:14:49.104 --> 00:14:49.771
page one lines ten through 15

00:14:49.771 --> 00:14:52.171
which have already been

00:14:53.575 --> 00:14:54.276
incorporated to clarify on this

00:14:54.276 --> 00:14:56.276
objective that enforcement

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:57.779
alone cannot eliminate the drug

00:14:57.779 --> 00:15:00.215
market and should be minimized

00:15:00.215 --> 00:15:00.949
whenever possible.

00:15:00.949 --> 00:15:01.616
This amendment reinforces our

00:15:01.616 --> 00:15:03.616
commitment to prioritizing

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:05.254
interagency collaboration,

00:15:05.254 --> 00:15:07.254
direct communication

00:15:08.624 --> 00:15:09.224
and deterrence over punitive

00:15:09.224 --> 00:15:09.825
measures while expanding

00:15:09.825 --> 00:15:11.825
pathways to employment

00:15:12.928 --> 00:15:13.629
education and rehabilitation

00:15:13.629 --> 00:15:16.290
for both nonviolent dealers

00:15:16.731 --> 00:15:17.990
and individuals struggling with

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:17.799
addiction.

00:15:17.799 --> 00:15:20.603
That clause now reads whereas

00:15:20.603 --> 00:15:21.304
dmi focuses the criminal legal

00:15:21.304 --> 00:15:23.704
system on disrupting public

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:24.874
markets by acknowledging that

00:15:24.874 --> 00:15:25.641
enforcement alone cannot

00:15:25.641 --> 00:15:28.641
eliminate the market and should

00:15:28.911 --> 00:15:29.545
be minimized whenever possible.

00:15:29.545 --> 00:15:31.545
Prioritizing interagency

00:15:32.648 --> 00:15:33.315
collaboration between law

00:15:33.315 --> 00:15:33.982
enforcement, public health

00:15:33.982 --> 00:15:36.382
and social service agencies

00:15:36.853 --> 00:15:37.387
replacing enforcement with

00:15:37.387 --> 00:15:37.987
direct communication

00:15:37.987 --> 00:15:39.987
and deterrence whenever

00:15:40.123 --> 00:15:40.790
feasible and providing

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.190
nonviolent dealers and users

00:15:44.293 --> 00:15:44.927
with pathways to employment,

00:15:44.927 --> 00:15:45.661
education, rehabilitation.

00:15:45.661 --> 00:15:47.830
I want to thank supervisor

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:48.531
fielder for recommending these

00:15:48.531 --> 00:15:50.931
amendments because it follows

00:15:51.834 --> 00:15:52.167
the spirit of where my focus is

00:15:52.167 --> 00:15:54.167
as well.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:55.672
>> I'd also today like to

00:15:55.672 --> 00:15:57.507
introduce three other non

00:15:57.507 --> 00:15:58.374
substantive amendments the

00:15:58.374 --> 00:15:59.209
first of which are on page two

00:15:59.209 --> 00:16:01.244
lines ten through 18 that will

00:16:01.244 --> 00:16:02.110
now read.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:04.547
Whereas the drug market agency

00:16:04.547 --> 00:16:05.314
coordination center launched

00:16:05.314 --> 00:16:06.480
in 2023 to enhance coordination

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.951
among the san francisco police

00:16:08.951 --> 00:16:09.685
department, san francisco

00:16:09.685 --> 00:16:12.850
district attorney's office, san

00:16:12.389 --> 00:16:13.123
francisco sheriff's department

00:16:13.123 --> 00:16:13.924
,department of public works

00:16:13.924 --> 00:16:16.559
and the department of emergency

00:16:16.559 --> 00:16:18.928
management has made significant

00:16:18.928 --> 00:16:19.629
progress including seizure of

00:16:19.629 --> 00:16:20.397
over 300 pounds of fentanyl

00:16:20.397 --> 00:16:23.232
and more than 2000 felony drug

00:16:23.232 --> 00:16:23.967
arrests.

00:16:23.967 --> 00:16:26.367
Whereas despite d-max efforts,

00:16:28.304 --> 00:16:29.138
enforcement is currently

00:16:29.138 --> 00:16:29.873
limited to 3 to 5 days per week

00:16:29.873 --> 00:16:31.808
underscoring the need for a

00:16:31.808 --> 00:16:32.442
sustained and comprehensive

00:16:32.442 --> 00:16:34.842
strategy to disrupt drug

00:16:35.512 --> 00:16:36.246
markets and illegal vending

00:16:36.246 --> 00:16:38.646
markets and reduce overdoses.

00:16:39.382 --> 00:16:40.150
>> and my last amendment will

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:43.860
delete part of the final clause

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:43.853
to now read as further resolved

00:16:43.853 --> 00:16:46.853
that the board of supervisors

00:16:47.291 --> 00:16:48.250
recommends allocating necessary

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.425
resources to fully implemented

00:16:50.594 --> 00:16:51.161
dmi strategy including

00:16:51.161 --> 00:16:51.895
increasing support for

00:16:51.895 --> 00:16:54.295
workforce and youth development

00:16:54.497 --> 00:16:55.198
programs and strengthening

00:16:55.198 --> 00:16:55.799
community based drug market

00:16:55.799 --> 00:16:57.799
disruption initiatives.

00:16:58.201 --> 00:16:58.902
I wanted to thank supervisor

00:16:58.902 --> 00:17:01.902
chen for these amendments to

00:17:01.971 --> 00:17:02.672
help the resolution focus on

00:17:02.672 --> 00:17:03.406
the spirit for which it is

00:17:03.406 --> 00:17:05.876
intended which is truly around

00:17:05.876 --> 00:17:06.610
deterrence and prevention.

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:09.100
This resolution can accordingly

00:17:10.147 --> 00:17:10.881
ensure that san francisco's

00:17:10.881 --> 00:17:13.817
using every tool available as

00:17:13.817 --> 00:17:14.551
the academic co-invented it

00:17:14.551 --> 00:17:17.551
describes as a harm reduction

00:17:17.854 --> 00:17:18.422
from the supply side to prevent

00:17:18.422 --> 00:17:19.890
harm and provide real

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.489
opportunities for our most

00:17:21.826 --> 00:17:22.627
vulnerable youth.

00:17:22.627 --> 00:17:23.227
>> because so many of the

00:17:23.227 --> 00:17:25.227
neighborhoods from the

00:17:25.563 --> 00:17:26.230
tenderloin to other

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:26.797
neighborhoods in the city

00:17:26.797 --> 00:17:27.431
deserve a childhood.

00:17:27.431 --> 00:17:29.299
And I'm grateful to my

00:17:29.299 --> 00:17:29.900
colleagues for recognizing this

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:30.568
fact and supporting the

00:17:30.568 --> 00:17:32.968
residents in any district.

00:17:33.336 --> 00:17:34.370
The dmi framework is an

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:34.705
evidence based model that has

00:17:34.705 --> 00:17:36.740
worked in cities across the

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.508
country.

00:17:37.508 --> 00:17:38.174
>> and it's time for san

00:17:38.174 --> 00:17:40.478
francisco to take action.

00:17:40.478 --> 00:17:41.245
It will take all of us to help

00:17:41.245 --> 00:17:43.748
build a safer, healthier future

00:17:43.748 --> 00:17:44.649
for all san franciscans.

00:17:44.649 --> 00:17:45.316
>> to that effect, I urge my

00:17:45.316 --> 00:17:47.118
colleagues to support this

00:17:47.118 --> 00:17:47.518
resolution as well.

00:17:47.518 --> 00:17:49.518
thank you.

00:17:50.988 --> 00:17:51.755
Supervisor mahmud there is a

00:17:51.755 --> 00:17:54.755
motion to amend the resolution

00:17:54.792 --> 00:17:55.559
before us.

00:17:55.559 --> 00:17:56.293
Is there a second for that?

00:17:56.293 --> 00:17:58.129
There's a second from

00:17:58.129 --> 00:18:00.129
supervisor dorsey

00:18:04.402 --> 00:18:04.702
and supervisor fielder I think.

00:18:04.702 --> 00:18:05.360
Yeah.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.360
Okay.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:09.640
Thank you supervisor mahmud for

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:09.974
bringing this resolution

00:18:09.974 --> 00:18:11.974
forward.

00:18:12.843 --> 00:18:13.511
>> I'm appreciative of the

00:18:13.511 --> 00:18:15.511
conversations we've had.

00:18:16.414 --> 00:18:17.480
To be clear, I did not advocate

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.480
for specific amendments.

00:18:20.585 --> 00:18:23.585
I expressed choose to reserve

00:18:24.756 --> 00:18:25.456
mahmud that the dmi strategy

00:18:25.456 --> 00:18:26.240
seems promising for holding

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:28.240
dealers accountable.

00:18:28.726 --> 00:18:29.427
However, I remain concerned

00:18:29.427 --> 00:18:31.827
that an enforcement approach

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.430
divorced from metrics related

00:18:36.201 --> 00:18:36.935
to public health goals street

00:18:36.935 --> 00:18:37.602
conditions will lead to just

00:18:37.602 --> 00:18:40.602
more arrests and jailing of

00:18:40.605 --> 00:18:43.541
drug users rather than dealers

00:18:43.541 --> 00:18:44.209
which ends up being so much

00:18:44.209 --> 00:18:44.909
more expensive for our city

00:18:44.909 --> 00:18:47.309
budget less consequential for

00:18:48.312 --> 00:18:48.946
public drug markets and more

00:18:48.946 --> 00:18:51.346
fatal for drug overdoses

00:18:51.517 --> 00:18:52.217
in scaling up respite centers

00:18:52.217 --> 00:18:52.951
and drug treatment because we

00:18:52.951 --> 00:18:55.951
have not adequately scaled up

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:56.421
respite centers and drug

00:18:56.421 --> 00:18:57.222
treatment.

00:18:57.222 --> 00:18:59.324
We continue to see displacement

00:18:59.324 --> 00:18:59.691
effects and increasing fatal

00:18:59.691 --> 00:19:00.425
overdoses.

00:19:00.425 --> 00:19:03.425
And now new research published

00:19:03.928 --> 00:19:04.562
just last week in the journal

00:19:04.562 --> 00:19:05.130
of the american medical

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.130
association and ising

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.268
specifically san francisco data

00:19:09.268 --> 00:19:12.271
shows that after a drug seizure

00:19:12.271 --> 00:19:12.905
overdose incidents increase

00:19:12.905 --> 00:19:15.305
during the next 24 hours

00:19:16.508 --> 00:19:17.575
and within 100m of the event.

00:19:17.575 --> 00:19:20.212
>> as long as we are unclear on

00:19:20.212 --> 00:19:23.682
the metrics along which we are

00:19:23.682 --> 00:19:24.383
measuring success and which

00:19:24.383 --> 00:19:26.783
initiatives or agencies are

00:19:27.386 --> 00:19:27.953
best suited for leading that we

00:19:27.953 --> 00:19:28.487
will continue to see

00:19:28.487 --> 00:19:30.487
displacement effects

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.525
and increased fatal overdoses.

00:19:32.525 --> 00:19:34.925
>> we need both enforcement

00:19:35.728 --> 00:19:36.395
and treatment if we want street

00:19:36.395 --> 00:19:37.950
conditions to improve and I

