00:28:22.294 --> 00:28:24.694
>> colleagues today I am

00:28:25.564 --> 00:28:27.564
introducing a resolution

00:28:29.202 --> 00:28:29.802
recognizing APRIL 2025 as

00:28:29.802 --> 00:28:31.802
national sexual assault

00:28:33.272 --> 00:28:33.773
awareness and prevention month

00:28:33.773 --> 00:28:35.773
in san francisco.

00:28:37.476 --> 00:28:38.277
I am deeply grateful that so

00:28:38.277 --> 00:28:41.280
many of my colleagues that this

00:28:41.280 --> 00:28:41.947
resolution has the support of

00:28:41.947 --> 00:28:42.247
so many colleagues on the

00:28:42.247 --> 00:28:42.948
board.

00:28:42.948 --> 00:28:44.951
We all recognize that sexual

00:28:44.951 --> 00:28:45.685
violence impacts people across

00:28:45.685 --> 00:28:48.850
all communities regardless of

00:28:48.655 --> 00:28:51.550
gender, race or age.

00:28:52.558 --> 00:28:53.493
It is a public health crisis

00:28:53.493 --> 00:28:56.329
that often begins early in life

00:28:56.329 --> 00:28:56.831
and carries devastating long

00:28:56.831 --> 00:28:58.831
term consequences.

00:29:00.633 --> 00:29:01.401
>> 1 in 9 girls, 1 in 20 boys

00:29:01.401 --> 00:29:03.801
will experience sexual assault,

00:29:04.504 --> 00:29:06.904
sexual abuse before adulthood.

00:29:07.474 --> 00:29:08.107
>> more than 2 million

00:29:08.107 --> 00:29:08.675
survivors of rape live

00:29:08.675 --> 00:29:10.675
in california today.

00:29:11.277 --> 00:29:11.944
These numbers are staggering

00:29:11.944 --> 00:29:14.944
but they are not abstract.

00:29:15.315 --> 00:29:15.982
They represent people in our

00:29:15.982 --> 00:29:18.982
city who live with trauma

00:29:19.319 --> 00:29:20.220
and deserve our support.

00:29:20.220 --> 00:29:20.921
Our job is to create a city

00:29:20.921 --> 00:29:23.321
that listens to survivors,

00:29:23.690 --> 00:29:24.391
believes them, ensures access

00:29:24.391 --> 00:29:26.893
to care and the justice that

00:29:26.893 --> 00:29:27.761
they need.

00:29:27.761 --> 00:29:30.497
>> we also have a duty to

00:29:30.497 --> 00:29:31.970
invest in prevention, education

00:29:31.970 --> 00:29:31.798
and early intervention

00:29:31.798 --> 00:29:34.198
especially for young people.

00:29:34.734 --> 00:29:35.468
This month is about raising

00:29:35.468 --> 00:29:35.802
awareness and recommitting to

00:29:35.802 --> 00:29:37.802
action.

00:29:39.439 --> 00:29:40.140
I want to express deep, deep

00:29:40.140 --> 00:29:42.876
gratitude to the people who

00:29:42.876 --> 00:29:43.543
show up every day for survivors

00:29:43.543 --> 00:29:45.543
the advocates, counselors,

00:29:47.800 --> 00:29:47.781
health care workers, teachers,

00:29:47.781 --> 00:29:50.181
case managers, family members

00:29:50.951 --> 00:29:51.718
and friends.

00:29:51.718 --> 00:29:52.485
They are often the first to

00:29:52.485 --> 00:29:54.722
hear the truth the first to

00:29:54.722 --> 00:29:55.456
offer care and the ones who

00:29:55.456 --> 00:29:58.425
walk with survivors through the

00:29:58.425 --> 00:29:59.293
hardest parts of healing.

00:29:59.293 --> 00:30:02.620
And I also want to thank the

00:30:02.620 --> 00:30:02.763
mayor's office of victims

00:30:02.763 --> 00:30:05.163
rights for their continued

00:30:06.330 --> 00:30:06.733
leadership in this work.

00:30:06.733 --> 00:30:09.350
And I want to recognize the

00:30:09.350 --> 00:30:09.636
youth commission for passing

00:30:09.636 --> 00:30:10.270
their own resolution

00:30:10.270 --> 00:30:10.904
and putting pushing this

00:30:10.904 --> 00:30:12.904
conversation forward with

