00:35:02.990 --> 00:35:05.269
This is also the year she

00:35:05.269 --> 00:35:05.769
became the chair of the first

00:35:05.769 --> 00:35:07.769
five commission.

00:35:09.574 --> 00:35:10.308
>> when she graduated with her

00:35:10.308 --> 00:35:10.908
new degree she started working

00:35:10.908 --> 00:35:12.710
with the san francisco

00:35:12.710 --> 00:35:13.444
department of public health

00:35:13.444 --> 00:35:16.113
initially as a contractor but

00:35:16.113 --> 00:35:16.848
then as a full time employee

00:35:16.848 --> 00:35:19.848
where she was tasked with

00:35:20.118 --> 00:35:20.852
finding ways to address the

00:35:20.852 --> 00:35:23.821
very troubling outcomes for san

00:35:23.821 --> 00:35:24.555
francisco's black mothers.

00:35:24.555 --> 00:35:27.555
What they were facing during

00:35:27.626 --> 00:35:30.626
pregnancy and birth in 2017 she

00:35:31.196 --> 00:35:31.896
started a collective impact

00:35:31.896 --> 00:35:34.296
effort that eventually gave

00:35:35.200 --> 00:35:35.967
rise to expecting justice a

00:35:35.967 --> 00:35:36.634
public health program that uses

00:35:36.634 --> 00:35:39.340
systems change and justice

00:35:40.400 --> 00:35:40.738
oriented approaches to

00:35:40.738 --> 00:35:43.138
dismantling racism and closed

00:35:43.408 --> 00:35:46.408
the racial gap in birth

00:35:47.245 --> 00:35:47.979
outcomes expecting justice work

00:35:47.979 --> 00:35:50.979
to advance access to community

00:35:51.449 --> 00:35:52.840
doulas a proven method of

00:35:52.840 --> 00:35:54.840
improving birth outcomes

00:35:55.654 --> 00:35:56.387
expecting justice also became a

00:35:56.387 --> 00:35:59.387
key partner in california's mom

00:35:59.691 --> 00:36:02.910
neighbors bill passed in 2021.

00:36:03.695 --> 00:36:04.363
This landmark legislation made

00:36:04.363 --> 00:36:07.363
full spectrum dual care a

00:36:07.499 --> 00:36:08.267
covered medical benefit.

00:36:08.267 --> 00:36:10.602
>> at that same year DR.

00:36:10.602 --> 00:36:11.269
Mallard won her expecting

00:36:11.269 --> 00:36:11.870
justice team launched the

00:36:11.870 --> 00:36:13.870
nation's first pregnancy

00:36:15.240 --> 00:36:15.941
guaranteed income program the

00:36:15.941 --> 00:36:18.341
abundant birth perk project.

00:36:18.844 --> 00:36:19.545
This pioneering program

00:36:19.545 --> 00:36:21.945
provides pregnant people who

00:36:22.514 --> 00:36:23.215
are at risk of birth

00:36:23.215 --> 00:36:25.615
disparities with a monthly

00:36:25.884 --> 00:36:26.652
income supplement.

00:36:26.652 --> 00:36:27.419
Beginning in san francisco, the

00:36:27.419 --> 00:36:29.819
abundant birth project provided

00:36:30.789 --> 00:36:33.189
mothers with a monthly $1,000

00:36:34.626 --> 00:36:35.327
for a year to help mothers

00:36:35.327 --> 00:36:37.727
buffer themselves against the

00:36:38.297 --> 00:36:38.864
impacts of structural

00:36:38.864 --> 00:36:40.864
and historical racism.

00:36:41.233 --> 00:36:41.934
>> in 2024 the abundant birth

00:36:41.934 --> 00:36:44.334
project expanded across the

00:36:44.804 --> 00:36:45.404
state to an additional four

00:36:45.404 --> 00:36:47.804
counties and today this

00:36:48.607 --> 00:36:51.700
pioneering program has given

00:36:51.977 --> 00:36:52.644
out nearly $5 million to 850

00:36:52.644 --> 00:36:55.644
pregnant people who are at

00:36:55.648 --> 00:36:56.149
highest risk of having

00:36:56.149 --> 00:36:56.916
premature births.

00:36:56.916 --> 00:36:59.986
Not only is this historic but

00:36:59.986 --> 00:37:00.753
it is also being replicated

00:37:00.753 --> 00:37:03.753
across the nation spurring a

00:37:04.724 --> 00:37:07.124
movement of providing pregnancy

00:37:08.393 --> 00:37:09.161
support to be kind

00:37:09.161 --> 00:37:09.495
and dignified in the care they

00:37:09.495 --> 00:37:11.495
deserve.

00:37:12.799 --> 00:37:13.533
>> sadly, there are many

00:37:13.533 --> 00:37:16.200
detractors who have also tried

00:37:16.200 --> 00:37:16.836
to sabotage this project.

00:37:16.836 --> 00:37:19.836
But DR. Malala is undeterred

00:37:20.106 --> 00:37:20.807
and continues her fight for

00:37:20.807 --> 00:37:23.207
public health programs that

00:37:23.910 --> 00:37:24.577
help marginalized families

00:37:24.577 --> 00:37:26.977
access necessary care that

00:37:28.130 --> 00:37:28.748
support the health of babies

00:37:28.748 --> 00:37:31.885
in that they are too often

00:37:31.885 --> 00:37:32.652
denied due to the structural

00:37:32.652 --> 00:37:33.190
and institutional barriers that

00:37:33.190 --> 00:37:35.190
they face.

00:37:36.155 --> 00:37:40.260
It is my honor to recognize DR.

00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:40.993
Malala into thank you and to

00:37:40.993 --> 00:37:43.629
recognize you in the movement

00:37:43.629 --> 00:37:44.363
you are leading for the

00:37:44.363 --> 00:37:47.363
countless lives you have saved

00:37:47.534 --> 00:37:48.135
and for your tireless work to

00:37:48.135 --> 00:37:48.535
advance racial justice

00:37:48.535 --> 00:37:50.535
in medicine.

00:38:00.380 --> 00:38:02.780
Thank you, DR. Malala.

00:38:04.551 --> 00:38:05.285
>> thank you so much

00:38:05.285 --> 00:38:05.952
supervisors thank you so much

00:38:05.952 --> 00:38:08.154
supervisor melgar for this

00:38:08.154 --> 00:38:08.955
great honor.

00:38:08.955 --> 00:38:09.890
I'm going to put on my glasses

00:38:09.890 --> 00:38:11.525
so I can actually read what I

00:38:11.525 --> 00:38:13.525
wrote.

00:38:14.928 --> 00:38:15.662
>> it feels amazing to have my

00:38:15.662 --> 00:38:18.620
contributions recognized in my

00:38:18.498 --> 00:38:19.265
hometown and to become part of

00:38:19.265 --> 00:38:19.832
a legacy of hard working women

00:38:19.832 --> 00:38:21.832
throughout this city.

00:38:23.370 --> 00:38:23.704
But even during women's history

00:38:23.704 --> 00:38:24.438
month as a pediatrician, I

00:38:24.438 --> 00:38:27.708
can't help but think about san

00:38:27.708 --> 00:38:28.375
francisco's future about the

00:38:28.375 --> 00:38:30.710
babies being born right now

00:38:30.710 --> 00:38:31.378
that will become the future

00:38:31.378 --> 00:38:33.778
inhabitants of this city.

00:38:34.281 --> 00:38:34.714
I'm worried for them

00:38:34.714 --> 00:38:35.382
in particular.

00:38:35.382 --> 00:38:38.219
I'm worried for our city's

00:38:38.219 --> 00:38:38.919
black babies because right now

00:38:38.919 --> 00:38:39.587
san francisco has the dubious

00:38:39.587 --> 00:38:41.987
distinction of having the

00:38:42.723 --> 00:38:44.959
highest black prematurity rate

00:38:44.959 --> 00:38:45.726
in the state.

00:38:45.726 --> 00:38:46.493
One out of every seven black

00:38:46.493 --> 00:38:49.290
babies in san francisco is born

00:38:49.290 --> 00:38:49.797
too early.

00:38:49.797 --> 00:38:50.464
Nearly twice the rate of san

00:38:50.464 --> 00:38:52.464
francisco's white newborns.

00:38:52.766 --> 00:38:53.400
Are you wondering how a city

00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:55.800
with world class medical

00:38:56.700 --> 00:38:56.838
institutions and an annual

00:38:56.838 --> 00:38:57.572
budget larger than some states

00:38:57.572 --> 00:39:00.508
is producing such poor health

00:39:00.508 --> 00:39:01.175
outcomes?

00:39:01.175 --> 00:39:02.900
>> the answer is racism.

00:39:02.900 --> 00:39:04.845
Too many black families in this

00:39:04.845 --> 00:39:05.512
city lack the resources needed

00:39:05.512 --> 00:39:07.912
to have healthy pregnancies

00:39:08.582 --> 00:39:09.350
and births as a pediatrician.

00:39:09.350 --> 00:39:12.219
>> I have too often seen black

00:39:12.219 --> 00:39:12.886
parents facing unimaginable

00:39:12.886 --> 00:39:13.521
stress because they cannot

00:39:13.521 --> 00:39:15.921
afford their basic needs.

00:39:16.357 --> 00:39:17.125
As a black mother and a long

00:39:17.125 --> 00:39:20.194
time resident I know this city

00:39:20.194 --> 00:39:20.895
offers black people so few

00:39:20.895 --> 00:39:22.895
opportunities for advancement

00:39:23.965 --> 00:39:24.465
and so many opportunities to

00:39:24.465 --> 00:39:24.932
experience racial

00:39:24.932 --> 00:39:25.633
discrimination.

00:39:25.633 --> 00:39:28.135
What would it look like for

00:39:28.135 --> 00:39:28.736
this city to truly invest

00:39:28.736 --> 00:39:29.690
in its black communities

00:39:29.690 --> 00:39:31.690
future?

00:39:32.340 --> 00:39:33.108
What would it look like to

00:39:33.108 --> 00:39:36.108
truly value this city's tiniest

00:39:36.111 --> 00:39:36.911
and most vulnerable residents?

00:39:36.911 --> 00:39:39.911
>> it might look something like

00:39:39.948 --> 00:39:40.715
the abundant birth project.

00:39:40.715 --> 00:39:41.349
When we first imagined the

00:39:41.349 --> 00:39:43.749
abundant burge project we

00:39:43.818 --> 00:39:44.485
imagined to san francisco where

00:39:44.485 --> 00:39:45.860
every parent can expect a

00:39:45.860 --> 00:39:47.486
joyful birth where every

00:39:48.356 --> 00:39:49.900
newborn can expect safe passage

00:39:49.900 --> 00:39:51.493
into the world where the future

00:39:51.493 --> 00:39:52.227
is bright because critical

00:39:52.227 --> 00:39:55.227
early investments have set the

00:39:55.363 --> 00:39:56.131
stage for a thriving society.

00:39:56.131 --> 00:39:58.667
