Thank you supervisor and guide

01:21:34.610 --> 01:21:36.610
you.

01:21:36.831 --> 01:21:39.831
>> at 86 I'm here for the

01:21:39.900 --> 01:21:42.900
historic perspective on women a

01:21:43.470 --> 01:21:44.171
very long time ago when I was

01:21:44.171 --> 01:21:47.508
just a small child there were

01:21:47.508 --> 01:21:50.978
few women heroes that could be

01:21:50.978 --> 01:21:51.679
served as models in when I was

01:21:51.679 --> 01:21:54.790
approximately six years old.

01:21:55.683 --> 01:21:56.250
>> I started settling.

01:21:56.250 --> 01:21:58.250
>> my women heroes.

01:21:59.853 --> 01:22:00.654
I chose florence nightingale

01:22:00.654 --> 01:22:03.525
because she went out into the

01:22:03.525 --> 01:22:04.125
battlefield to care for the

01:22:04.125 --> 01:22:06.525
sick and the wounded.

01:22:07.228 --> 01:22:08.620
>> I chose annie oakley because

01:22:08.620 --> 01:22:11.662
she was a really good horse

01:22:11.833 --> 01:22:14.802
rider and she won all of her

01:22:14.802 --> 01:22:17.202
shooting contests against men.

01:22:18.606 --> 01:22:19.306
>> I chose eleanor roosevelt

01:22:19.306 --> 01:22:19.707
because she was known for her

01:22:19.707 --> 01:22:21.707
good works.

01:22:23.440 --> 01:22:23.812
>> and though I was a little

01:22:23.812 --> 01:22:25.947
fuzzy on what good works were,

01:22:25.947 --> 01:22:26.714
I thought that was something

01:22:26.714 --> 01:22:30.685
good to be in my own family.

01:22:30.685 --> 01:22:33.685
>> there have been women heroes

01:22:34.922 --> 01:22:35.589
much lesser accomplishment than

01:22:35.589 --> 01:22:38.293
those I've named yet still

01:22:38.293 --> 01:22:40.693
remarkable for their time.

01:22:41.463 --> 01:22:42.297
>> my great great grandmother

01:22:42.297 --> 01:22:45.297
fleeing a famine and a

01:22:48.403 --> 01:22:50.403
turbulent political society

01:22:52.173 --> 01:22:52.907
left europe to cross the ocean

01:22:52.907 --> 01:22:56.211
and come to new york and then

01:22:56.211 --> 01:22:56.945
from new york to go overland to

01:22:56.945 --> 01:22:59.715
the midwest to marry a widower

01:22:59.715 --> 01:23:00.716
twice her age.

01:23:00.716 --> 01:23:04.316
>> she was a mail order bride.

01:23:07.322 --> 01:23:08.230
I am the proud, great great

01:23:08.230 --> 01:23:10.230
granddaughter of immigrants

01:23:13.462 --> 01:23:17.620
and I have never forgotten that

01:23:17.533 --> 01:23:20.803
I have an aunt, a great aunt

01:23:20.803 --> 01:23:24.403
who walked the streets to help

01:23:24.473 --> 01:23:24.706
women to have the right to vote

01:23:24.706 --> 01:23:26.706
.

01:23:28.777 --> 01:23:32.377
>> I have a grandmother who was

01:23:33.820 --> 01:23:33.849
the first woman to own a car

01:23:33.849 --> 01:23:37.190
in the county she lived in and

01:23:37.190 --> 01:23:37.953
my own mother who had a tender

01:23:37.953 --> 01:23:41.230
age of 13, was sent off to

01:23:41.230 --> 01:23:43.859
boarding school so that she

01:23:43.859 --> 01:23:47.459
could become the first in her

01:23:47.729 --> 01:23:48.631
family to become a teacher.

01:23:48.631 --> 01:23:51.567
>> women have come a long way

01:23:51.567 --> 01:23:52.568
in seeking their heroes today.

01:23:52.568 --> 01:23:55.568
>> the field is much broader

01:23:56.380 --> 01:23:56.705
and the examples that we have

01:23:56.705 --> 01:23:57.390
to look to are much more

01:23:57.390 --> 01:23:59.390
diverse.

01:23:59.842 --> 01:24:00.543
