01:24:00.543 --> 01:24:02.943
software engineers, ceos of

01:24:03.745 --> 01:24:04.646
companies.

01:24:04.646 --> 01:24:07.684
>> we even came close to having

01:24:07.684 --> 01:24:08.510
a woman PRESIDENT In my

01:24:08.510 --> 01:24:10.510
lifetime.

01:24:11.254 --> 01:24:12.880
>> please.

01:24:12.880 --> 01:24:14.891
>> as I progressed through my

01:24:14.891 --> 01:24:15.725
chosen careers I was almost

01:24:15.725 --> 01:24:18.725
warned about a glass ceiling.

01:24:21.730 --> 01:24:22.298
This was a term coined in 1978

01:24:22.298 --> 01:24:22.966
and it came to mean

01:24:22.966 --> 01:24:25.966
in referring to a supposed

01:24:26.436 --> 01:24:26.836
limitation on professional

01:24:26.836 --> 01:24:28.836
advancement.

01:24:30.240 --> 01:24:33.240
>> yes, there have been clear

01:24:33.676 --> 01:24:34.310
instances in my career when

01:24:34.310 --> 01:24:37.310
I've been the only woman

01:24:37.513 --> 01:24:38.247
present in a group of males

01:24:38.247 --> 01:24:41.318
when I've been the only woman

01:24:41.318 --> 01:24:44.318
who stood up and spoke.

01:24:45.188 --> 01:24:45.756
>> but those days are gone.

01:24:45.756 --> 01:24:46.423
